---
import Document from "@/layouts/Document.astro";
import { LAB, OPERATOR } from "@/lib/site";
---

<Document
  title="Disclaimer"
  heading="Disclaimer"
  description="letsauth.eu is an independent project. It does not speak for any employer or vendor and takes no money for listings. Its data is reference material, with no security advice and no certification."
  path="/disclaimer/"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lede={`${LAB} is an independent project. It speaks for no employer and no vendor. What it publishes is reference material and gives no advice.`}
  updated="2026-10-22"
>
  <h2>No employer affiliation</h2>
  <p>
    letsauth is a personal project. I, {OPERATOR.name}, build it in my own time to make agent
    authentication easier to understand. Everything here reflects my own views and my experience
    in usable security and web authentication. I do not speak for the company I work
    for, or for any company I worked for in the past, and nothing on this site is an official
    position of any of them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Links and discussion are welcome. If you quote or refer to the site, please name{" "}
    {LAB} or me without a company affiliation.
  </p>

  <h2>No vendor affiliation, no paid placement</h2>
  <p>
    letsauth carries no advertising, no affiliate links and no sponsored content. No vendor pays
    to be listed, to be left out, or to see a cell change. Servers are listed in alphabetical
    order and nothing is scored or ranked. Where a cell comes from a vendor's own documentation,
    it is marked as a vendor claim.
  </p>

  <h2>Reference material, not advice</h2>
  <p>
    We compile the atlases with care from specifications, vendor documentation, public
    directories and passive reads of public metadata. Each cell shows its source, method and
    date. Products change and observations age, so a cell can be out of date or wrong. An{" "}
    <em>unknown</em> cell says only that no observation is on record. The site is not a security
    audit, a certification or a compliance statement for any product. It does not replace your
    own assessment. Please <a href="/contribute/">send a correction</a> when you
    find a mistake.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    The content is provided as is, without warranty. Liability for its accuracy, completeness
    or timeliness is excluded as far as the law permits. This does not affect liability for
    intent and gross negligence, or for injury to life, body or health.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to specifications, vendor pages and repositories run by others. Their
    owners are responsible for them. When a link was added, the target showed no apparent
    breach of law. We do not monitor linked pages continuously. If you notice a link to unlawful
    content, tell us and we will remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>Names and marks</h2>
  <p>
    Product, company and specification names and logos are the property of their owners and are
    used only to identify what is described. Their use does not imply endorsement in either
    direction.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{OPERATOR.email}</a> or read who runs the site
    on the <a href="/about/">about page</a>.
  </p>
</Document>
